1
00:04:33,103 --> 00:04:39,103
Long live the king.

2
00:09:06,206 --> 00:09:12,206
Godzilla: King of the Monsters is a science fiction,
action film directed by Michael Dougherty.

3
00:13:39,310 --> 00:13:45,310
Follows the heroic efforts of the crypto-zoological agency Monarch as its members face off against a battery of god-sized monsters,
including the mighty Godzilla, who collides with Mothra, Rodan, and his ultimate nemesis, the three-headed King Ghidorah.

4
00:18:12,413 --> 00:18:18,413
When these ancient super-species, thought to be mere myths, rise again, they all vie
for supremacy, leaving humanity's very existence hanging in the balance.

5
00:22:45,517 --> 00:22:51,517
Mark Russell, played by Kyle Chandler.

6
00:27:18,620 --> 00:27:24,620
Emma Russell, played by Vera Farmiga.

7
00:31:51,724 --> 00:31:57,724
Madison Russell, played by Millie Bobby Brown.

8
00:36:24,827 --> 00:36:30,827
Dr. Ishiro Serizawa, played by Ken Watanabe.

9
00:40:57,931 --> 00:41:03,931
Dr. Ilene Chen / Dr. Ling, played by Zhang Ziyi.

10
00:45:31,034 --> 00:45:37,034
Dr. Rick Stanton, played by Bradley Whitford.

11
00:50:04,137 --> 00:50:10,137
Godzilla: King of the Monsters is a 2019 American monster film produced
by Legendary Pictures and distributed by Warner Bros.

12
00:54:37,241 --> 00:54:43,241
Co-written and directed by Michael Dougherty, it is a sequel to
Godzilla (2014) and the third film in the Monsterverse.

13
00:59:10,344 --> 00:59:16,344
It is also the 35th film in the Godzilla franchise, and the third
Godzilla film to be completely produced by a Hollywood studio.

14
01:03:43,448 --> 01:03:49,448
The film stars Kyle Chandler, Vera Farmiga, Millie Bobby Brown, Bradley Whitford, Sally Hawkins, Charles Dance,
Thomas Middleditch, Aisha Hinds, O'Shea Jackson Jr., David Strathairn, Ken Watanabe, and Zhang Ziyi.

15
01:08:16,551 --> 01:08:22,551
In the film, eco-terrorists release King Ghidorah, who awakens other monsters known as "Titans" across the
world, forcing Godzilla and Mothra to surface and engage Ghidorah and Rodan in a decisive battle.

16
01:12:49,655 --> 01:12:55,655
The sequel was greenlit during the opening weekend of Godzilla, with
Gareth Edwards expected to return to direct a trilogy.

17
01:17:22,758 --> 01:17:28,758
In May 2016, Edwards left the project.

18
01:21:55,862 --> 01:22:01,862
In October 2016, Dougherty and Shields were hired to rewrite the script.

19
01:26:28,965 --> 01:26:34,965
In January 2017, Dougherty was announced as the director.

20
01:31:02,068 --> 01:31:08,068
Principal photography began in June 2017 in Atlanta,
Georgia, and wrapped in September 2017.

21
01:35:35,172 --> 01:35:41,172
The film is dedicated to executive producer
Yoshimitsu Banno (director of Godzilla vs.

22
01:40:08,275 --> 01:40:14,275
Hedorah) and original Godzilla suit performer Haruo
Nakajima, both of whom died in 2017.

23
01:44:41,379 --> 01:44:47,379
Godzilla: King of the Monsters was theatrically released on May 31, 2019, to mixed reviews from critics, with praise for its visual
effects, action sequences, cinematography, and musical score but with criticism to the plot, pacing, tone and characters.

24
01:49:14,482 --> 01:49:20,482
The film was a box office disappointment, grossing $387.3 million worldwide against a production budget of $170–200
million and marketing costs of $100–150 million, marking it the lowest-grossing film in the Monsterverse.

25
01:53:47,586 --> 01:53:53,586
A sequel, Godzilla vs.

26
01:58:20,689 --> 01:58:26,689
Kong, was released on March 24, 2021.

27
02:02:53,793 --> 02:02:59,793
The film explores themes of mexico, boston, massachusetts,
giant monster, cryptozoology, eco terrorism.

28
02:07:26,896 --> 02:07:32,896
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
